s Management and organisation Submenu for Management and organisation Lund University is seeking a new Deputy Vice-Chancellor to take office on 1 January 2027 University Management Submenu for University Management Vice-Chancellor Erik Renström Deputy Vice-Chancellor Lena Eskilsson Pro Vice-Chancellor Ann Kristin Wallengren Pro Vice-Chancellor Jimmie Kristensson Pro Vice-Chancellor Kristina Eneroth Pro Vice-Chancellor Per Mickwitz Pro Vice-Chancellor Viktor Öwall University Director Susanne Kristensson University Board Organisational structure Global engagement Submenu for Global engagement Global Africa Asia Europe Submenu for Europe Erasmus+ Latin America North America Oceania Research collaboration Submenu for Research collaboration Strategic collaboration agreements KIC – Knowledge and Innovation Communities Work for us Submenu for Work for us Working at Lund University Vacancies Applying for a job Career paths Submenu for Career paths Doctoral student Academic roles Researcher roles Professional services roles Living and working in Sweden Contact us Submenu for Contact us International Office Press Office Supplier portal Collaborate with us Recruit our students Social media Visit the University Submenu for Visit the University Campus locations Lund, Skåne and Sweden Experience the University Submenu for Experience the University Museums, collections and archives Arts, music and theatre Lund University Shop Giving to Lund University Submenu for Giving to Lund University Different ways to support us Contact the Development Office The University in a turbulent world Submenu for The University in a turbulent world FAQs regarding the war between Israel and Hamas Support for students Career paths at Lund University På svenska Lund University offers a variety of career opportunities, including academic, research, doctoral and professional service roles. Whatever your expertise, you can develop your skills and contribute to the University's work. Being employed as a doctoral student As a doctoral student at Lund University, you are employed while completing your doctoral (PhD) studies. This gives you financial security and full employee benefits. The role combines research training with opportunities for teaching or departmental duties, preparing you for a career in academia or beyond. Employment as a doctoral student Working as an academic At Lund University, academic roles combine education and research. The University offers a clear career path from assistant lecturer to professor. This provides long-term stability, opportunities for promotion and the chance to shape both students' learning and the University's research environment. Working in academic roles Working in a research role At Lund University, if you primarily work in research, you can focus on advancing your research through dynamic projects and international collaborations. Research positions are often project-based and not always permanent. Working in researcher roles Working in professional services roles As administrative and technical staff, you play a vital role in supporting research, education and daily operations across the University. These roles offer stable employment, opportunities for professional development and the chance to contribute your expertise in a collaborative environment. Working in professional services roles Academic career paths Academic career paths in Sweden follow a structure aligned with the European framework for academic careers and tenure-track positions. They progress from doctoral student to postdoctoral researcher or associate senior lecturer (assistant professor), then to senior lecturer or researcher, and eventually to professor. Academic career paths at Lund University View job vacancies We advertise positions in academic, research, doctoral and professional services roles. Most of the job listings published in English don't require knowledge of Swedish. Subscribe to job alerts To receive daily emails or weekly summaries of vacancies in your chosen job categories, subscribe in Varbi. Contact information Human Resources webbansvarig@hr.lu.se Postal address Box 117 221 00 Lund Sweden Lund University on LinkedIn Last updated: \n    29 Aug 2026 Faculties Faculty of Engineering, LTH Faculty of Fine and Performing Arts Faculties of Humanities and Theology Faculty of Law Faculty of Medicine Faculty of Science Faculty of Social Sciences School of Economics and Management, LUSEM All faculties and departments Institutes and centres Institutes and Research Centres Cultural and Public Centres University administration University Management International Office Press Office Contact information Box 117, 221 00 Lund, Sweden Telephone: +46 (0)46 222 00 00 (switchboard) Invoice address: Box 188, 221 00 Lund Organisation number: 202100-3211 Contact us Shortcuts Webmail Privacy policy About this website Cookie policy Accessibility statement Giving to Lund Find us on social media Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Collaboration and networks Back to top"
