 overall assessment of teaching qualifications includes higher education pedagogy training, teaching experience and teaching expertise. Experience of teaching and course development in Economic History with a focus on development economics, labour markets, colonialism and long-term development processes is considered a merit. Consideration will also be given to how the applicant’s experience and expertise may complement and strengthen education and research within the Department. Application The application must include: Cover letter CV and list of publications Description of teaching and research qualifications, maximum three pages One selected paper (working paper or publication, as a link or PDF) Degree certificates, etc. Applicants are encouraged to provide the names and contact details of a maximum of two persons who can provide references. Letters of recommendation will not be considered as part of the application. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Employment expires 2026-12-31 Contract type Full time Salary Månadslön Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2185 Contact Anna Tegunimataka, +46462220498, anna.tegunimataka@ekh.lu.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 01.Sep.2026 Last application date 22.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
